From 54688c7bf47979cd4d718ed5eabfad9bb998f55d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aliaksei Ivanou <aliaksei.ivanou@innowise.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:47:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Report nested missing assertions once per attempt

With retries enabled, TAP wrote the 'Attempt k of M failed:' heading before every diagnostic of a superseded attempt; it now writes it once per attempt. JUnit and SonarQube labelled a missing-assertion failure in a leaf section as 'no assertions in test case'; they now say 'no assertions in section' when the test case itself had assertions. Regenerate the amalgamated sources.

Tests: exhausted and fail-then-pass nested-section NoAssertions scenarios for the recorder, JUnit, SonarQube, TeamCity, and TAP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GunDRycct3rWzK5p7dpZxP
